// many-heads — the ONLY fixture that reaches the prose cap, and the only one
// that can test the completeness claim at bs_diag.erl:1100-1101 ("the prose and
// the term channel cannot say different things"). On CONTENT that is true. On
// COMPLETENESS it is false by design and nothing tested it: this residual is
// five heads, the prose prints three and a `... (2 more)` line, and the term
// channel carries all five.
//
// Nine fixtures produce exactly one head each, so without this one the cap
// branch of the channel check would ship never having executed — the shape of
// defect check-language.sh has, where `seq 1 0` iterates nothing and exits 0.
//
// It doubles as the atom-union-in-one-head row: `:b1 | :b2 | :b3` inside a
// single head does not parse, and that is a different route to `|` than the
// binary tag fixture takes.
module ManyHeads

type A = :a1 | :a2 | :a3
type B = :b1 | :b2 | :b3
type C = :c1 | :c2 | :c3

public atom Trip(A x, B y, C z)
Trip(:a1, :b1, :c1) -> :hit
Trip(:a2, :b2, :c2) -> :hit2
